# GRC Portfolio

Governance, risk, and compliance projects I've built to apply what I'm 
learning through my B.S. in Cybersecurity (USF) and my work as an Internal 
Compliance Auditor. Each project is based on a real company, a real 
incident, or a real framework. The reasoning is to give my own personal take
on each incident or organization and what I would personally recommend
based on what I know. 

Every project is always open to new suggestions that will help me grow as
a professional.

## Projects [Including those in progress]

### [Vendor Risk Policy - EY Breach](./01-vendor-risk-policy-ey-breach)
Third-party vendor risk management policy written in response to the 2026 
Ernst & Young data breach. Built around NIST SP 800-161 and NIST SP 800-53, 
with controls mapped directly to the actual incident timeline and root cause.

### Risk Register - Lithia Motors *(in progress)*
Enterprise risk register for a public automotive retailer, built from their 
actual SEC 10-K risk disclosures using NIST IR 8286 methodology.

### SOC 2 Gap Assessment - Okta *(in progress)*
Control maturity assessment against the AICPA Trust Services Criteria, 
using Okta's public Trust Center controls and their documented 2022/2023 
security incidents to identify where stated controls didn't hold up in practice.

## Background

B.S. Cybersecurity, University of South Florida (Dec 2026) — Minor in 
Professional & Technical Communications. CompTIA CSAP (Security+ & CySA+), 
AWS Solutions Architect – Associate. Currently working as an Internal 
Compliance Auditor.

